{
    "background_story": "Alice was an Egyptologist with a passion for uncovering the secrets of the ancient gods. Her fascination with Thoth, the patron deity of wisdom and magic, led her to spend years studying the mystical texts and hieroglyphs left behind by the Egyptians. As she delved deeper into her research, Alice began to experience strange and vivid dreams, which she believed were messages from Thoth himself. She became convinced that the god was guiding her towards a long-lost temple hidden deep in the desert. Undeterred by skepticism and danger, Alice embarked on a perilous journey to find the temple, driven by her devotion to Thoth and her thirst for knowledge. Her discovery of the temple and its ancient secrets would go on to rewrite the history of Egyptology, cementing Alice's reputation as a brilliant and fearless scholar.",
